# Findings this repository has looked at and decided not to block on, with the
# reason and a date on which the decision expires.
#
# THE RULE FOR THIS FILE. An entry is allowed only when the vulnerable code is
# present and NOT REACHABLE in the way the advisory requires — never because a
# fix is inconvenient, and never without an `exp:` date. The date is the point:
# an accepted finding that cannot go red again is an accepted finding nobody
# will look at twice. When it expires the build fails, and that is the intended
# behaviour.
#
# Trivy already runs with `ignore-unfixed: true` (.github/workflows/ci.yml), so
# anything listed here is a finding upstream HAS fixed and we are carrying on
# purpose. That is a higher bar than "no patch exists yet" and this file must
# stay short.

# No entry today. The last one -- CVE-2026-14456, openssl in node:24-alpine --
# expired on 2026-09-23 and was answered the way its own note said to answer
# it: the digest was bumped, not the date.

